														<td valign="top">
															
															During a raid I was invited to with a high-end guild, I experienced something I would like to share that may have use to DOR raids.<br /><br />The necros had their own channel. Healers said in raid channel they're state of mana. When a healer said /rs 15m , it was the necros as a group who were responsible for twitching. The organization was great. All the necros created a hotkey that consisted of essentially :<br /><br />/# TWITCHING &lt;NAME&gt; (where # is the number of necro channel)<br />/cast #<br />/pause 40<br />/cast #<br />(where # is the number of the spell gems for the 2 twitch spells we have)<br /><br />So, as you can see, we accomplish twitching the requester AND&nbsp;telling the other necros who we're twitching. There is ABSOLUTELY no reason to inform the person being twitched as they either know or don't know by the casting messages they receive if they are being twitched or not.<br /><br />Also, since the necro Lifeburn AA does not stack, we used this channel to announce to each other when Lifeburn was used and when the recourse effect faded, so that Lifeburn was not wasted.<br /><br />It is acceptable for the healers to join the channel if they wish but it is not necessary. All we as necros need to know is the state of mana i.e /rs 20m. We can take it from there.<br /><br />If anyone starts saying, well, we can't rely on&nbsp;all necros to twitch when healers are lom, then we need to seriously ask ourselves if those necros should even be in the raid. After raiding several of the EP's and PoTime, I can tell you, that every necro in the raid needs to be ready and willing to twitch on a second's notice as the raid will expect you to do it and do it NOW!&nbsp;<br /><br />As for spam during battle, get used to it. In the EPs and such, things happen so fast, that if you lack the ability to catch a /tell, /rs 15m, or can't open the alt-r window to target a healer to twitch, you will be missing a very important part of your job as a&nbsp;necro in raid. As the raid is forming, you need to have a good handle on what healers are in which group. Members of the CCH take priority for twitches. If need be, write down they're name and group # to be able to target faster....better yet, create a hotkey to target them instantly. Healers have a lot to do in the raid and a lot to watch....we necros on the other hand, typically do 2 things....DPS and Twitch.<br /><br />A note about DPS.....A good Necro will NEVER get summoned and NEVER get agro....if you don't have it, work on getting Spell Casting Subtley 3. Also, know your spells, which create huge agro and which don't. For instance, don't ever re-cast your rune-type spell after casting a chain of DoTs....you will almost indubitably get agro. Make copious use of FD and/or Death Peace AA (frees spell slot) to drop agro after casting. Be aware of when a tank falls in battle and FD or stop casting until the SA grabs agro. Everyone knows Necros can get agro....don't prove it in raid.<br /><br />Ty for reading this long post and I hope it helps. <br /><br />-R-<br />
