														<td valign="top">
															
															<p>1 other thing I wanted to add:<br /><br />DOR has or2:1, as a permanently moderated channel, because people couldn't seem to get it through their heads that /rs is for raid information only. There were too many buff requests and general chitchat going on in the channel. This continues to this day, albeit a bit less. My frame of view comes from guild raids, where /rs is holy ground, reserved solely for raid information. Channels, /tell, and /gu are for chitchat and even that is kept to a minimum during raid. So clerics giving their state of mana in /rs is really no issue, as NO ONE else in the raid can do anything about it, except a necro and it's not like you have 40 healers spamming the channel with their mana states.</p>
