													<tr>
														<td valign="top">
															
															I personally feel that the handling of twitches is something that the necros and healers should get together to work out a process for.&nbsp; The reasons being<br /> 1) I am neither a necro nor a healer and therefore have no idea what the pros and cons of a given system are as far as actual implement-ability on a raid itself and<br /> 2) When different systems have been suggested in the past typically either the healers and/or necros say it's a rotten idea and they flat out won't do it and<br /> 3) Everything seems more credible when it's suggested by someone who actually plays the class being affected by the idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe the problem is that as of yet our healers haven't needed twitches on a given raid.&nbsp; Sunscape is, I think, the only healer who has posted to this thread, and she said things are working fine (albeit that was some time ago).&nbsp; That being said, I know that at the very least for certain fights (Xegony) we will need a solid twitch plan.&nbsp; Many ideas here and previously suggested are decent:<br /> <br /> A) Have a twitch channel - Necros join and monitor the channel. Healers join and filter the channel to a spam window and just have a hotkey saying /# --Need Twitch--.<br /> pro: Necros can see twitch requests without being spammed<br /> con: Healers have to join another channel, keep track of the number, and make sure their hotbutton is always going to that channel.<br /> <br /> B) Have necros join the heal channel - Healers announce their twitch needs in heal channel (so it stands out, eg ---TWITCH---).<br /> pro: minimizes total number of channels anyone has to be in<br /> con: necros have to monitor CH spam to see twitch needs.<br /> <br /> C) Assign certain healers to certain necros at the beginning of the raid. Healers make a hotbutton to /tell NecroX --Twitch please--<br /> pro: tells are usually the easiest thing for people to see, you know 5 necros aren't twitching the same healer.<br /> con: we typically have far fewer necros than healers. Healers have to change their hotbutton every raid.<br /> <br /> D) Have healers announce mana in rsay, necros have twitch channel to coordinate.<br /> pro: healers don't have to join a channel, necros don't have to monitor spam (rsay should be relatively clear)<br /> con: As Gold said, we'll have some yahoo's spamming their mana as soon as they see a cleric do it, and rsay won't remain clear.<br /> <br /> So...the healers I talked to flat out refused to go with option A.&nbsp; The necros I spoke to flat out refused to go with option B (although at least at the time Sun posted, some necros each raid did do option B and it appeared to be working out ok).&nbsp; Option C has a lot more cons that I listed and I personally don't think it's the best way to go (again, I'm neither a healer nor necro).&nbsp; Option D would probably be the option we'd be most likely to be able to convince people to actually do since necros don't seem opposed to having a twitch channel and few healers, I would guess, would be opposed to announcing their mana in rsay.<br /> <br /> Again, I think this is a debate best left to the healers and necromancers to decide, if y'all think we need a necro lead to coordinate with Sun I'll be more than happy to appoint one.&nbsp; If it can't be agreed on and it becomes a problem, then I'll be happy to choose one or the other (which I'm sure as usual everyone will disagree with ;) .&nbsp; I do think the coordinating of twitches is important, but again since Sun posted and no healers have since had trouble (that I'm aware of) I assumed everything was trundling along nicely :) .<br /> 
