															As of now, I simply join the heal channel and monitor that, as it's not an issue at the level of raiding that DOR is doing atm. As I am not a DOR lead, nor do I wish to be one, due to the fact I cannot devote the time necessary to do the job right, I am open to any system everyone wants. Having used every system mentioned, Option D works the best, providing everyone in the raid knows that only healers have leave to state mana levels in /rs and that only healers will be receiving twitches <em>during </em>battle. Twitch requests for the rest of raid can be by /tell. <br /><br />People have learned to use /tell for buff requests, they can use /tell for twitch requests during down time. Only healers should have leave to use /rs for mana state. <br /><br />I am flexible to what everyone wants to do, just let us know and I'll follow along with the system you wish, even if Jetta decides :)<br />
