														<td valign="top">
															
															SCS affects a DoT's first tick only. It does not affect further ticks.<br /><br />And we do get aggro from DOT crits.<br /><br />And I *have* been to a DOR raid or two. I agree that our twitch system doesn't work. I've suggested several mechanisms that were deemed unacceptable by clerics.<br /><br /><br />I do not want to have to read a spammed channel to pick out "twitch please". If it is that important, then we can set up a mechansim for it.<br /><br />I have suggested hotkeys for tells. This works partiularly well becuase it means the necro can do /rt to get the requestor targeted. Since OR's very first raid, I have had ongoing "relationships" with many clerics and others that set up such keys and they do get twitched. Yes, I acknowledge that this does not scale well and is less than optimal as a general solution, but of all mechanisms, this gets the fastest response because of the fact we can /rt.<br /><br />Again, what I'd like to see is an ORNECRO channel that Necros can monitor. Clerics (and others) can send twitch requests into this channel. Nobody other than necros need to monitor the channel, it could be redirected to a minimized window.<br /><br /><br />As for the statement that the target of the twitch does not need to know that they're being twitched or by whom? The "twitchee" *has* to be told (and periodically reminded). A Necro has no way to tell the target's mana status. The target can go FM and the twitch still goes off, the necro does not know this. I have hotkeys that I use to let the target know that they are being twitched and requesting that the target /reply when they have enough mana. I've watched too many people go AFK after requesting twitching, come back and say "oh, I've been FM for awhile". Gee. Thanks.<br />
